course: dictionary
lesson: 15741
title: Trapped: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Trapped» is the past form of the verb trap, and it can also be an adjective. Its main meaning is caught so that you cannot get away or get out. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The kitten was trapped under the fence.» The kitten cannot get out, so trapped means stuck.
explain: The same word can mean different things. «The mouse was trapped in the cage.» Here trapped means caught in a trap. «The warm air was trapped in my thick coat.» Here trapped means held in one place, so the air could not escape. Ask yourself: what is trapped, and where?
explain: Feeling trapped is about a situation, not a place. «Mia felt trapped by her homework, with no way out.» Nobody locked Mia in a room. She felt she had no way out of a bad situation.
fact: Trapped means caught so that you cannot get away or get out.
fact: «Trapped» can be a verb (the past form of trap) or an adjective.
fact: «Trapped air» means air held in one place, so it cannot escape easily.
fact: Air trapped in fur, feathers or double glazing helps keep things warm, because it does not let heat out easily.
fact: Never hide in an old fridge, car boot, chest freezer or lift, because you could get trapped. If you are trapped in a lift, press the alarm and wait.
exercise: «The kitten was trapped under the fence.» What does trapped mean here? | Sleeping in the sun | Happy and playing | *Stuck, and unable to get out | Washed clean
exercise: «The warm air was trapped in my thick coat.» What does trapped mean here? | Blown away by the wind | Made into a cold drink | Painted bright red | *Held in one place, so it could not escape
exercise: «Lily felt trapped by the long list of chores.» What does feeling trapped mean? | Feeling cold in the snow | *Feeling she has no way out of a bad situation | Feeling very tired after a nap | Feeling brave enough to climb a tree
test: «The fox was trapped by the farmer's wire in the night.» What does trapped mean here? | Feeling sad and alone | Held in a warm coat | Running fast through the field | *Caught in a trap, as an animal can be
test: «If you are trapped in a lift, what should you do?» | Climb through the ceiling | Jump out through the doors | Hide under the seat | *Press the alarm and wait
exam: «The air trapped in the double glazing keeps the room warm.» What does trapped mean in this sentence? | Caught in a net by a fisher | *Held in one place, so the heat cannot easily escape | Feeling sad about the cold | Locked inside a cupboard
